EXT. FERRIS WHEEL - TOP CABIN - NIGHT

The wheel has stopped at its peak. The city glitters below. Wind rocks the cabin. A duffel bag lies open on the bench.

FENELLA (30s, black turtleneck) is hunched over a thermal drill. RAUL (40s, sunglasses even now) peers out of the window, scanning the ground. ABIOLA (20s, headset) mutters coordinates into a radio. NOLAN (50s, ex-operator's jacket) sits slumped with his feet on the duffel.

She jabs the drill at the floor. He jerks the curtain. She curses. He snaps his fingers.

FENELLA
Hold it still.

RAUL
I'm holding.

ABIOLA
Wind's rising. Four knots.

NOLAN
We said sixty seconds.

FENELLA
We said sixty seconds yesterday.

RAUL
We said sixty seconds before you spilled the thermite.

ABIOLA
Everyone, quiet. Security's on the midway.

They freeze. Beneath them the wheel creaks. She taps her earpiece. He holds his breath. They all lean toward the window as a flashlight beam sweeps the base of the wheel.

NOLAN
(whisper)
Don't breathe.

FENELLA
(whisper)
Then who's talking?

RAUL
(whisper)
You are.

The beam passes. The wheel jolts. The cabin begins, very slowly, to descend.
